message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "TCM Symptom Ontology (TCM-SO): a large-scale bilingual ontology of Traditional Chinese Medicine symptoms with HPO / SNOMED CT / ICD-11 alignment"
abstract: >-
  A large-scale, bilingual (Chinese/English) OWL 2 ontology of Traditional Chinese
  Medicine (TCM) symptoms. The release contains 1,938 classes (1,758 symptom
  classes in 31 clinical categories) with 15,199 subclass axioms and 12,928
  existential restrictions, bilingual labels on 100% of classes, and English
  textual definitions for 93.1% of symptom classes (50.4% manually translated).
  Ten equivalence axioms and one property chain provide GO-style faceted
  classification along an anatomical finding-site axis, orthogonal to the
  asserted clinical-workflow category hierarchy. Cross-terminology alignment,
  confirmed by TCM domain experts, covers 649 HPO, 707 SNOMED CT and 973 ICD-11
  mappings; 979 of 1,758 symptom classes (55.7%) align to at least one external
  terminology. Logical consistency verified with HermiT (0 unsatisfiable classes).
